license: MIT

abstract: >-
  PerturbContextAlign provides analysis code for studying how pretrained text
  encoders represent single-cell perturbation context and how semantic
  relationships in those representations correspond to experimentally measured
  perturbation responses. The released analyses cover context retention,
  text-response correspondence, controlled context and mechanism perturbations,
  and downstream prediction-oriented evaluations across genetic, small-molecule,
  and combination perturbation datasets.

keywords:
  - "single-cell perturbation"
  - "single-cell RNA sequencing"
  - "perturbation context"
  - "pretrained text encoders"
  - "text embeddings"
  - "representation learning"
  - "perturbation response"
  - "response alignment"
  - "drug perturbation"
  - "genetic perturbation"

